as in April 2025.","context":"Rooms revenues","section":"Results of Operations","block":349,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-051092","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001616000","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1616000/000162828026051092/xhr-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/32eefb0806188feb8fc18cf83e628506b34abd58d18bdcbeaa5804a38a37886e.bin","sha256":"32eefb0806188feb8fc18cf83e628506b34abd58d18bdcbeaa5804a38a37886e"}},{"id":"4e265405b3371dc7d56835dfd7c924d4ac7977ba1a83890daaf81d4b0c008e0d","quote":"Rooms revenues increased $12.7 million, or 4.0%, to $331.0 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026 from $318.4 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 primarily driven by increases in occupancy and average daily rate as well as year over year growth at Grand Hyatt Scottsdale Resort due to continued ramp up in performance following the renovation. This increase is net of a reduction of $7.5 million attributed to the sale of Fairmont Dallas in April 2025.","context":"Rooms revenues increased $8.2 million, or 5.2%, to $166.7 million for the three months ended June 30, 2026 from $158.5 million for the three months ended June 30, 2025 primarily driven by increases in occupancy and average daily rate as well as year over year growth at Grand Hyatt Scottsdale Resort due to continued ramp up in performance following the renovation. This increase is net of a reduction of $0.7 million attributed to the sale of Fairmont Dallas in April 2025.","section":"Results of Operations","block":350,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-051092","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001616000","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1616000/000162828026051092/xhr-20260630.htm"