 three months ended June 30, 2026 from $102.2 million for the three months ended June 30, 2025 primarily driven by an increase in occupancy and year over year growth at Grand Hyatt Scottsdale Resort due to continued ramp up in performance following the renovation. This increase is net of a reduction of $0.7 million attributed to the sale of Fairmont Dallas in April 2025.","section":"Results of Operations","block":354,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-051092","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001616000","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1616000/000162828026051092/xhr-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/32eefb0806188feb8fc18cf83e628506b34abd58d18bdcbeaa5804a38a37886e.bin","sha256":"32eefb0806188feb8fc18cf83e628506b34abd58d18bdcbeaa5804a38a37886e"}},{"id":"808853a960cb5a2640aaa55a96d5ac54e728c03e988a212200983c0bb939f898","quote":"Other revenues increased $1.2 million, or 2.3%, to $52.4 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026 from $51.3 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 primarily due to increases in occupancy and ancillary fees as well as year over year growth at Grand Hyatt Scottsdale Resort due to continued ramp up in performance following the renovation. This increase is net of a reduction of $0.9 million attributed to the sale of Fairmont Dallas in April 2025.","context":"Other revenues decreased $0.5 million, or 1.9%, to $26.4 million for the three months ended June 30, 2026 from $26.9 million for the three months ended June 30, 2025 primarily due to a $0.4 million reduction in other revenues from cancellations and attrition for our comparable hotels as well as a $0.1 million reduction attributed to the sale of Fairmont Dallas in April 2025.","section":"Results of Operations","block":357,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verifi